  "term": "hihat",
  "says": "A closed hi-hat, Reid's cymbal recipe cut short: noise (or a cluster of inharmonic squares, the metal) through a high-pass so only the top is left, an instant attack and a decay of a few tens of milliseconds; the open hat is the same with the decay stretched. Signature: nearly all energy above 4 kHz, a flat spectrum, an attack under 5 ms, -20 dB within 150 ms.",
